  "_calibration": "Calibrated in Godot 4.7.2 (Forward+, D3D12) with lookdev capture --probes. Exteriors on an open ground plane, interior_daylight in a 8x6x3 m room with one 2x1.6 m window. Relative mode: clear_midday key 1.06 / key-fill 2.5 stops; golden_hour 1.02 / 2.6; overcast 0.60 / 0.3 (lookdev 0.8.0: exposure 0.75, grey probe 0.56 display; 1.0 read 0.60, over the 0.58 limit); night 0.20 / 3.1; interior median display luma ~0.25. Physical mode: clear_midday key 1.20 / 2.3; golden_hour ~1.0 / ~2.3; overcast ~0.7 / 1.1 (measured before 0.8.0, not re-measured); night 0.17 / 3.0; interior median ~0.43. Godot's physical exposure lands about one stop darker than Sunny-16 arithmetic predicts, hence 1/60 s at f/16 for midday sun. Scenes with dark ground, heavy occlusion or big interiors will differ: re-measure and move exposure first."
